    "instruction": "Could you use the CDC Child and Teen BMI Calculator? Use US Customary Units; enter Girl age 12 years 0 months, 5 ft 0 in, 120 lbs. Calculate. In Spreadsheet set: A1='Field', B1='Value', A2='BMI', B2=<copy displayed BMI>, A3='BMI Percentile', B3=<copy displayed percentile exactly>, A4='Category', B4=<copy displayed category>, A5='Rounded BMI', B5='=ROUND(B2,0)', A6='Category Flag', B6='=IF(B4=\"Underweight\",\"LOW\",IF(B4=\"Healthy Weight\",\"OK\",IF(B4=\"Overweight\",\"WATCH\",IF(B4=\"Obesity\",\"HIGH\",\"SEVERE\"))))'. Check B5 and B6. Save `~/Documents/cdc_child_teen_bmi_010.docx` in the format 'Scenario: [value] | BMI: [value] | BMI Percentile: [value] | Category: [value] | Rounded BMI: [value] | Category Flag: [value]'. Word format: line 1 title bold+underlined 16pt; body 12pt regular.",
